Senior Healthcare Integration Engineer – Rhapsody / HL7 / .NET
Location: Idaho (Remote – Local Candidates Preferred)
Duration: 12 Months

Interview: Webcam or In-Person

Job Description
We are seeking a Senior Healthcare Integration Engineer with strong hands-on experience in Rhapsody Integration Engine, HL7, IDSS, and .NET technologies. The candidate will support existing healthcare integration systems, troubleshoot public health data exchange workflows, and contribute to legacy system modernization initiatives.

Key Responsibilities
Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot Rhapsody interfaces and HL7 integrations.
Manage healthcare data exchanges between external organizations, DPH, and CDC.
Support and maintain NEDSS Base System (NBS), NBS Utilities, and ELR data store.
Develop and maintain C#/.NET applications, SQL queries, and PowerShell scripts.
Support eCR and ELR workflows and implement system upgrades.
Administer Windows Server and IIS environments.
Participate in system modernization, architecture planning, and technology evaluations.
Coordinate with hospitals, laboratories, CDC, and internal teams.

Required Skills
Rhapsody Integration Engine – 3+ years
SQL Development & Troubleshooting – 3+ years
eCR – 2+ years
ELR – 2+ years
HL7 or FHIR – 2+ years
Azure DevOps – 2+ years
C# / .NET Framework
PowerShell Scripting
Requirements Analysis and Critical Thinking

Nice-to-Have Skills
Oracle PL/SQL
NBS/NEDSS Systems
IIS Configuration and Windows Server Administration
TFS, SMTP, and SFTP
LOINC, SNOMED, and ICD-10-CM
Public Health Data Exchange Experience

